For fair comparison:
The same model, temperature, and generation parameters are used for both conditions.
7. Evaluation Metrics
7.1 Compilation Success Rate
Measures whether generated tests can compile successfully without modification.
Formula:
Compilation Rate =

Compiled Generated Tests /
Total Generated Tests
7.2 Test Execution Success
Measures whether generated tests successfully execute in the target environment.
Metrics:
Passing tests
Runtime failures
Assertion failures
7.3 Code Coverage
Measures how much production code is exercised by generated tests.
Metrics:
Line coverage
Function coverage
Branch coverage
7.4 Mock Generation Accuracy
Evaluates whether generated mocks correctly represent architectural abstractions.
Metrics:
Correct protocol mocking
Dependency replacement accuracy
Avoidance of concrete implementation usage
7.5 Architectural Compliance Score
Measures whether generated tests respect architectural constraints.
Evaluation criteria:
Criterion	Description
Dependency inversion	Uses abstractions instead of concrete classes
Layer isolation	Does not violate module boundaries
Mock strategy	Uses appropriate dependency replacement
Concurrency handling	Correctly handles async/MainActor requirements


