9. Threats to Validity
Internal Validity
Potential issues:
randomness of LLM generation,
prompt sensitivity,
model updates.
Mitigation:
multiple generation runs,
fixed prompts,
controlled model parameters.
External Validity
Potential issues:
limited number of programming languages,
Swift-focused evaluation.
Mitigation:
The proposed framework is language-independent at the conceptual level and can be extended to other languages supporting modular architectures.
Construct Validity
Potential issues:
automated metrics may not fully represent test quality.
Mitigation:
Combine automated measurements with manual architectural evaluation.
10. Expected Outcome
The expected outcome of this experiment is to determine whether architecture-aware context engineering improves LLM-based unit test generation quality compared to code-only approaches.
The experiment aims to demonstrate that providing structured architectural knowledge enables LLMs to better understand software structure, dependency relationships, and testing requirements.